Subject: [PATCH] webgpu: request the depth32float-stencil8 device feature

Forward+ allocates its depth-stencil target as D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT. WebGPU
exposes that combined format only behind the optional device feature
depth32float-stencil8, and asking for it without enabling the feature does not
produce a validation error -- createRenderPipeline throws:

  TypeError: Failed to execute 'createRenderPipeline' on 'GPUDevice': Use of the
  'depth32float-stencil8' texture format requires the 'depth32float-stencil8'
  feature to be enabled

A thrown TypeError stops the renderer outright rather than failing one pipeline,
so nothing after it draws.

The JS shell already builds an optional-feature list and filters it against
adapter.features, so this is one entry in that list; adapters without the
feature are unaffected. Forward Mobile never requested a stencil alongside a
32-bit depth buffer, which is why the gap only surfaces once Forward+ gets far
enough to create its depth attachment.

diff --git a/platform/web/js/engine/engine.js b/platform/web/js/engine/engine.js
--- a/platform/web/js/engine/engine.js
+++ b/platform/web/js/engine/engine.js
@@ -319,6 +319,13 @@
 			// Request optional texture format tiers used by Godot (r16snorm, rg16snorm, etc.).
 			var optionalFeatures = [
 				'readonly-and-readwrite-storage-textures',
+				// Forward+ allocates its depth-stencil target as D32_SFLOAT_S8_UINT,
+				// which WebGPU exposes only behind this optional feature. Without it
+				// createRenderPipeline throws a TypeError -- not a validation error --
+				// and the whole renderer stops before drawing. Forward Mobile never
+				// asked for a stencil alongside a 32-bit depth, which is why the gap
+				// only appears now.
+				'depth32float-stencil8',
 				'texture-formats-tier1',
 				'texture-formats-tier2',
 				'float32-filterable',
